#: ../../source/docs/common-ek3-affinity-lane-switching.rst:89
#: 96c1e8e1121049c5869aa63f521640d5
msgid "An example of lane switching for a plane with 2 GPS and GPS affinity enabled. There are 2 IMUs, hence 2 active lanes. The primary lane's GPS is simulated with a random GPS Velocity Noise of range ±2m in all 3-axis. The actual speed can be tracked with the 2nd GPS. Subsequently, the EKF primary lane starts reporting a consistently high error and a lane switch occurs when the error crosses the set threshold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ek3-affinity-lane-switching.rst:95
